{"url":"https://roboticoverlords.org/tinyhat","guid":"https://lobste.rs/s/mbm7xw","feedId":"lobsters","source":"Lobsters","publisher":null,"category":"tech","title":"Tiny Hat: a new Linux distro dedicated to retro gamedev","summary":"Tiny Hat uses only around 100MB of RAM after booting, and can be booted from a >= 1GB memory stick. It comes with a few small games, an easy way to install and run more games and several example programs for getting into retro game development. It also uses a modern stack of libraries, with dwl / Wayland, SDL3 and GTK4. One possible use is to buy a cheap x86 machine to younger members of a family, to completely brain wash inspire them into getting into graphics programming and appreciating retro games, perhaps as a Christmas present. At least a few people has found it fun so far, so I wanted to share it. Comments","content":"","caption":"","authors":["roboticoverlords.org by xyproto"],"tags":["linux","games","retrocomputing"],"publishedAt":"2026-11-27T09:11:13.000Z","updatedAt":null,"firstSeenAt":"2026-11-27T09:24:59.241Z"}
